      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torrance%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community sits on the south side of the Conemaugh River, just 2.2 miles east of Blairsville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Torrance%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Torrance Historical Society & Museum promotes local history through research, archives, and a museum open Wednesdays, Thursdays, and Sundays.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://torrancehistoricalsociety.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Society runs a Plaque Program that places bronze plaques on significant historic landmarks throughout Torrance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://torrancehistoricalsociety.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Society hosts annual events like Rock Around the Block and Historic Home Tour, drawing visitors to Old Torrance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        6
